  "description": "An ocular-ergonomic color system engineered from retinal neurobiology and myopia prevention research (Aleman, Wang & Schaeffel, 2018, Nature Scientific Reports 8:10840).",
  "research_grounding": {
    "citation": "Aleman, A. C., Wang, M., & Schaeffel, F. (2018). Reading and Myopia: Contrast Polarity Matters. Scientific Reports, 8:10840. DOI:10.1038/s41598-018-28904-x",
    "retinal_pathway": "Stimulates the retinal ON-pathway through positive contrast polarity, promoting choroidal thickening (+10 µm) and inhibiting scleral axial elongation, while bounding syntax within a 515-590 nm spectral corridor to eliminate longitudinal chromatic aberration (LCA < 0.35 D).",
    "sunlight_resilience": "Nature Light features a calibrated diffuse parchment baseline (L=0.88) to overpower ambient window glare without triggering the severe -16 µm choroidal thinning of blinding 100% white."
